    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4ca9f73ac7e369bf",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4ec348834c93842a467c69d8655dcbe72aa47092fa7d2c31ff3909ab13c72a50",
      "text": "The excursion lasts about **6–8 hours** and is led by an English-speaking guide.\n\nThe Argentine side of Iguazú Falls has numerous walking trails and footbridges over the water. You can see the falls from both upper and lower levels.\n\nAlong the park trails, you may see orchids, birds, reptiles and other rainforest wildlife.\n\nA highlight is the ride on the ecological train followed by a walk to the Devil’s Throat viewing platform, which overlooks the most powerful cascade in the falls.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-mw6m9wxh-cczxw4dr6hs0t03up1hi6je",
        "model": "GPT-6.1-sol"
      }
    },
    {
